Feature visualization
=====================

Reproduction source code for the article _A Survey of Activation Maximization_
at https://henrikaalto.fi/blog/feature-visualization.

Each chapter has a Python module that should be ran from the repo's root with uv.

Main Timeline
-------------

2009: First Images
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.first_images_2009

2013: Weight Decay
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.weight_decay_2013

2014: Total Variation
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.total_variation_2014

2015: Gaussian Blur
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.gaussian_blur_2015

2015: Random Shifts
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.random_shifts_2015

2017: Fourier
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.fourier_2017

2023: MACO
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.maco_2023

2026: Path Guidance
    <omitted>

Other techniques
----------------

2016: DGN-AM
    uv run --locked python -m weights.dgn
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.dgn_am_2016

2018: CPPNs
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.cppns_2018

2022: Masked Autoencoders
    uv run --locked python -m weights.mae
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.masked_autoencoders_2022

2024: DiG-IN
    uv run --locked python -m recipes.dig_in_2024

Assets
------

The Inception weights were extracted from the frozen Lucid graph:
https://storage.googleapis.com/modelzoo/vision/other_models/InceptionV1.pb

The fixed magnitude prior is from Xplique. Its source, checksum, and
license are in assets/maco_imagenet.json.

See LICENSES/ for the upstream notices. Additional model downloads are
cached outside the tracked files.
